KSTATION6","channel":"System","event_id":7040,"label":"service start type changed","fields":{"param1":"Microsoft NDIS Capture","param2":"system start","param3":"demand start"},"count":1,"fleet":22}],"split":"test","answer_key":{"gold":["T1047"],"title":"Covenant SharpWMI Exec","description":"This dataset represents an adversary remotely executing code via WMI. This dataset focuses on the use of the WMI Win32_Process class and method Create to execute code remotely.","dataset":"SDWIN-200806035621","recording":"covenant_sharpwmi_create_dcerpc_wmi_2020-08-06035621"},"nightwatch":{"techniques":["T1134.005","T1053.005","T1071.001"],"verdict":{"assessment":"An adversary executed a Grunt HTTP2 C2 agent via WMI on WORKSTATION6, established command and control communications, and modified a scheduled task on the domain controller (MORDORDC) to execute CompatTelRunner with system privileges for reconnaissance and persistence.","findings":[{"technique_id":"T1134.005","name":"SID-History Injection","parent":"Access Token Manipulation","tactics":["Stealth","Privilege Escalation"],"behavior":"GruntHTTP2.exe accessed registry keys and attempted privilege escalation operations using SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege on named objects.","slot":1,"reasoning":"The evidence shows GruntHTTP2.exe attempting to use SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege on named objects (\\Device\\ConDrv and \\BaseNamedObjects\\RasPbFile), which is characteristic of token impersonation or privilege escalation via access token manipulation. This is distinct from registry modification alone\u2014the process is attempting to take ownership of system objects to escalate privileges, which maps to Access Token Manipulation rather than the registry modification or COM techniques offered.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E015","field":"PrivilegeList","quote":"SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege","ok":true},{"event_id":"E016","field":"ObjectName","quote":"\\BaseNamedObjects\\RasPbFile","ok":true},{"event_id":"E015","field":"ProcessName","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\GruntHTTP2.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1053.005","name":"Scheduled Task","parent":"Scheduled Task/Job","tactics":["Execution","Persistence","Privilege Escalation"],"behavior":"A scheduled task (Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser) was modified on MORDORDC and CompatTelRunner.exe executed with SYSTEM privileges to access LSA and telemetry controller registry keys for reconnaissance.","slot":2,"reasoning":"The evidence shows a scheduled task (Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser) was modified and then executed with SYSTEM privileges via svchost.exe. This is task scheduling abuse for execution, not reconnaissance\u2014the registry access to LSA keys is incidental to the task's normal operation after modification. T1053.005 is the most specific technique for scheduled task modification and execution.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E038","field":"TaskName","quote":"\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Application Experience\\Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser","ok":true},{"event_id":"E031","field":"NewProcessName","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\CompatTelRunner.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E031","field":"ParentProcessName","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1071.001","name":"Web Protocols","parent":"Application Layer Protocol","tactics":["Command and Control"],"behavior":"WmiPrvSE.exe spawned GruntHTTP2.exe which initiated outbound HTTP connections to 10.10.10.5:80 and performed DNS queries, establishing command and control communications.","slot":0,"reasoning":"The evidence shows GruntHTTP2.exe initiating outbound HTTP connections to 10.10.10.5:80, which is the primary objective\u2014establishing command and control via HTTP application layer protocol. While DNS queries are present, they appear incidental (querying the local hostname); the HTTP connection to a remote IP on port 80 is the actual C2 channel being established.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E004","field":"Image","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\GruntHTTP2.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1}],"unverified":[],"declined":[],"hypotheses":[{"behavior":"WmiPrvSE.exe spawned GruntHTTP2.exe which initiated outbound HTTP connections to 10.10.10.5:80 and performed DNS queries, establishing command and control communications.","event_ids":["E004","E017","E019"],"keywords":["WMI execution","C2 agent","HTTP beaconing","DNS query","Grunt"]},{"behavior":"GruntHTTP2.exe accessed registry keys and attempted privilege escalation operations using SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege on named objects.","event_ids":["E009","E010","E015","E016"],"keywords":["privilege escalation","registry access","SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege","named objects"]},{"behavior":"A scheduled task (Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser) was modified on MORDORDC and CompatTelRunner.exe executed with SYSTEM privileges to access LSA and telemetry controller registry keys for reconnaissance.","event_ids":["E038","E031","E043","E044"],"keywords":["scheduled task modification","persistence","SYSTEM privilege","LSA registry access","reconnaissance"]}],"retried":[]},"trace":[{"t":2.39,"agent":"hunter","kind":"text","text":"I'll analyze this alert systematically, starting with the triage view to identify the key adversary behaviors."},{"t":2.41,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"search_events","result":{"matches":90,"events":"<log_events trust=\"untrusted\">\n[E004] +19s WORKSTATION6 Sysmon 1 process created: User=THESHIRE\\pgustavo IntegrityLevel=High ParentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\wbem\\WmiPrvSE.exe Image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\GruntHTTP2.exe CommandLine=\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\GruntHTTP2.exe\"\n[E005] +19s WORKSTATION6 Sysmon 1 process created: User=THESHIRE\\pgustavo IntegrityLevel=High ParentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\GruntHTTP2.exe Image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\conhost.exe CommandLine=\"\\??\\C:\\windows\\system32\\conhost.exe 0xffffffff -ForceV1\"\n[E006] +19s WORKSTATION6 Sysmon 10 process accessed: SourceImage=C:\\windows\\system32\\wbem\\wmiprvse.exe Targe