s modified (E038) and CompatTelRunner.exe was launched with system privileges. This process:\n   - Accessed LSA registry keys (E043, E044)\n   - Accessed multiple telemetry controller registry keys (E045-E049)\n   - Created and deleted registry keys in a user registry hive (E040-E042)\n\nThe pattern suggests: WMI-based execution of a C2 agent (Grunt), lateral movement to another workstation, and persistence/reconnaissance on the domain controller via scheduled task manipulation."},{"t":11.19,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"set_model_response","result":{"assessment":"An adversary executed a Grunt HTTP2 C2 agent via WMI on WORKSTATION6, established command and control communications, and modified a scheduled task on the domain controller (MORDORDC) to execute CompatTelRunner with system privileges for reconnaissance and persistence.","hypotheses":[{"behavior":"WmiPrvSE.exe spawned GruntHTTP2.exe which initiated outbound HTTP connections to 10.10.10.5:80 and performed DNS queries, establishing command and control communications.","event_ids":["E004","E017","E019"],"keywords":["WMI execution","C2 agent","HTTP beaconing","DNS query","Grunt"]},{"behavior":"GruntHTTP2.exe accessed registry keys and attempted privilege escalation operations using SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege on named objects.","event_ids":["E009","E010","E015","E016"],"keywords":["privilege escalation","registry access","SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege","named objects"]},{"behavior":"A scheduled task (Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser) was modified on MORDORDC and CompatTelRunner.exe executed with SYSTEM privileges to access LSA and telemetry controller registry keys for reconnaissance.","event_ids":["E038","E031","E043","E044"],"keywords":["scheduled task modification","persistence","SYSTEM privilege","LSA registry access","reconnaissance"]}]}},{"t":11.19,"agent":"hunter","kind":"output","output":{"assessment":"An adversary executed a Grunt HTTP2 C2 agent via WMI on WORKSTATION6, established command and